  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-10-30T06:18:07.504Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I can completely understand that not all bugs can be found before a release. Bugs are bound to occur no matter how much time the patch spends in Beta testing. But you should ALWAYS assume that gamebreaking bugs will happen.\nYou should never release a patch less than a week before one of the biggest holiday and most anticipated events in the entire game/platform/community, or even in the entire gaming genre in the world.\nAny other company could and would tell you the same. I'm just asking for better planning in the future because this recent patch has completely destroyed majority if not all planned community events that were supposed to happen for Halloween. All thanks to bad planning.\nNot putting anyone down, just general feedback.",
